  selPause:(n)=>`Pause selected (${n})`, selResume:(n)=>`Resume selected (${n})`,
  pauseTip:'Pause physics = pin the whole physics group with engine fixed constraints, then clear all linear and angular velocity.\nEverything inside keeps running: Create machines spin, fluids flow, hoppers pull.\n\nResume only releases the pin; ticking and force-load state are untouched. Persists across restarts.',
  freezeBody:'❄ Pause ticking', thawBody:'☀ Resume ticking', frozenTag:'Ticking paused (whole group halted)',
  stateNeedsLoad:'Force-load the whole physics group first',
  selFreeze:(n)=>`Pause ticking (${n})`, selThaw:(n)=>`Resume ticking (${n})`,
  freezeTip:'Pause ticking = stop block-entity ticking for the whole physics group.\nCreate machines, fluid networks and hoppers all stop, but physics keeps running — nothing is pinned, velocity is kept.\n\nUse "Pause physics" when the group must stand still. Persists across restarts.',
  thawT:'Resume ticking',
  thawMsg:(n,m,b)=>`Resume ticking for the physics group of "${n}": ${m} bodies, ${fmt(b)} blocks total.\n\nOnce the group runs again, Create machinery and the physics solver come back at the same time.\nAt this scale that has been measured to overwhelm the main thread until the watchdog kills the server.\n\nResume anyway?`,
  thawSelMsg:(n,m,b)=>`Resume ticking for the physics groups of ${n} selected bodies, affecting ${m} bodies / ${fmt(b)} blocks.\n\nRestarting a large group risks overwhelming the main thread and crashing the server. Resume anyway?`,
  forceBody:'Force-load', unforceBody:'Cancel force-load', forcedTag:'Force-loaded by panel', forcedBadge:'Force-loaded',
  selForce:(n)=>`Force-load selected (${n})`, selUnforce:(n)=>`Cancel force-load (${n})`,
  forceHint:'Force-load = attach a sable force-load ticket to the whole physics group so it stays loaded and runs naturally.\nDoes not clear velocity, pin physics or pause ticking. If the group contains detached debris you are asked about cleanup first.\n\nCancelling only exits force-load: the running state is saved and the whole group unloads to disk; pause-physics / pause-ticking intents are kept and re-apply on next load. Tickets survive restarts.',
  forceCopiesFirst:'This group has multiple disk copies: pick the primary version in "Manage copies" first, then force-load',
  forcedLostBadge:'Force-load lost', forcedLostTag:'The intent exists but the ticket is gone. If the body was permanently removed, background revival stops to avoid another removal loop.\nForce-load again to retry explicitly, or cancel force-load to clear the intent.',
  forcedExternalBadge:'Externally loaded', forcedExternalTag:'Running, but not kept by a panel force-load: chunk loaders, tickets from other mods/commands, or a player nearby all count.\nCancelling force-load has no effect here — the green dot is controlled by the external source.',
  clearVelTip:'Clear all linear and angular velocity of the group; it stops right where it is.\nDoes not pause physics or ticking — gravity and collisions still act afterwards.\nOnly affects loaded members.',
  clearVelNeedsLoad:'No loaded members in this group: for cold bodies use Teleport instead (it clears velocity and saves to disk)',
  autoRepairGroup:'Auto-repair physics group', autoRepairing:'Auto-repairing…', autoRepairT:'Auto-repair physics group',
  autoRepairHint:'Loops automatically: clean trusted detached debris, force-load, keep the single runtime-proven primary version, verify the whole physics group.\nStops when positions are ambiguous, member details are incomplete or no unique primary exists — never guesses, never restores from the recycle bin.',
  autoRepairMsg:(n,m,d,c)=>`Auto-repair the physics group of "${n}".\n\nCurrently visible: ${m} members, ${d} detached, ${c} members with copy anomalies.\nThe flow cleans trusted detached debris, force-loads, keeps the single runtime-proven primary version and verifies, converging in at most 3 rounds. Removed data still enters the recycle bin first, and the panel never auto-restores.\n\nStops immediately whenever evidence is not unique or any step is incomplete. Start?`,
  autoRepairDone:(m,d)=>`Auto-repair finished: ${m} members${d?`, cleaned ${d} detached`:''}`,
  autoRepairFailed:'Auto-repair stopped: ', autoRepairPartial:'Not every sub-operation succeeded',
  autoRepairForceCopies:'Force-load did not succeed. This group has copy members: if the reason is "cannot pick a force-load version", choose the complete disk version in "Manage copies" first; details in the job log',
  autoRepairMissing:'This physics group no longer exists',
  autoRepairTruncated:'Member details are truncated; the whole physics group cannot be handled safely',
  autoRepairUnsure:'The anchor position is ambiguous; cannot safely tell which members are detached',
  autoRepairUnsureConfirm:(n)=>`\n\n⚠ The anchor has several disk copies at different positions; the ${n} detached members are judged against the position the list uses. Continuing means you confirm these really are debris; the flow stops if the detach list changes at all before writing.`,
  autoRepairNoVersion:'No complete primary version; auto-repair will not quarantine unique data',
  autoRepairCopyLoss:(n)=>`The primary version would still remove ${n} currently running members; review the impact in "Manage copies" and confirm manually`,
  autoRepairEvidenceIncomplete:(n,m)=>`Only ${n}/${m} running members have activity evidence; cannot pick a primary version automatically`,
  autoRepairChanging:'The physics group still had not converged after 3 rounds',
  autoRepairRefreshTimeout:'Timed out waiting for the physics group to refresh',
  detachedBadge:'Detached', detachedTag:'Bounding box no longer connects to the anchor — debris left behind where a physics bearing broke.\nIt still counts as part of the physics group, so force-load is forced to pin it in memory too.',
  detachedT:'Clean detached debris',
  detachedMsg:(n,total,drop,blocks,keep)=>`The group of "${n}" has ${total} bodies; ${drop} of them no longer connect to the anchor, ${fmt(blocks)} blocks total.\n\nThese are debris left where physics bearings broke (often hundreds to thousands of blocks away), but sable still counts them in the same physics group — without cleanup, force-load has to pin all ${total} bodies in memory.\n\nThis deletes ${drop} and keeps ${keep}. Everything is backed up to the recycle bin first and can be restored any time.\n\nClean and continue?`,
  detachedUnsure:'⚠ The anchor itself has several disk entries at different positions — the judgement pivots on one of them; picking wrong swaps what to keep with what to delete.\nLoad the group first (teleport there and take a look): loaded bodies use live coordinates, and only then does the judgement count.',
  detachedTruncated:(n)=>`This group has ${n} detached debris, but member details were truncated and the list is incomplete.\nAuto-cleanup would only delete half, so nothing is touched here.\n\nForce-load the whole group anyway? (debris gets pinned in memory too)`,
  detachedPartial:'Not all debris was cleaned (see the failure message — usually disk copies with different content; handle them in "Manage copies" first).\n\nThe remaining debris still rides along with force-load — attaching tickets synchronously pulls chunks thousands of blocks away, which has been measured to stall the main thread and crash the server.\n\nContinue force-loading anyway?',
  delConfirmT:'Delete body', delConfirm:(n,b)=>`Delete "${n}"? This body has ${fmt(b)} blocks.\nIt is backed up to the recycle bin first and can be restored any time.`,
